S3a - LCDCalc v1.0 - Freeware - (c) Marko Schuster 1996

This program needs GTLib v1.0 (which can also be found in this
LCDCalc.zip - archive)


What?
-----

LCDCalc is a Calculator with a big LCD (40 pixel height font!) and all
functions on a one-key-press, a numeric-like keypad, ...



Install?
--------

Copy lcdcalc.opa to one of your \app\-directories and dig40m.fon in a
\fon\-directory on M: A: or B:. 

And of course be sure you have installed GTLib. GTLib was written
by me, so I don't have to write much about here ;-)


Usage
-----

Ok, after start you'll see a LCD-alike-display and the keyboard-layout.
If you don't use a english or german keyboard, this layout may be wrong.
As used just work with the prg. as a normal calculator. In the line
above the display you can see the expression which will be calculated when
you press = or RETURN. In the line under the display you will see the
mode for hex/dec/bin and deg/rad and also the 6 memories M1-M6. These
memories are shared with the built-in calculator, the memories also
will not lose their contents by quitting the programm. Access the memories
with the menu or Psion-Hotkeys. 

Keys
----

1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 9 0 / * - + = ,/.  ( )      what do you think, eh? ;-)

q=log  w=ln  e=e^x  r=square-root  t=tan  z(y)=arctan  u=4  i=5  o=6  p=x^y

a=arcsin   s=sin   d=deg/rad    f=(    g=)   h=hex/dec/bin   j=1   k=2   l=3

y=x!   x=Quit   c=cos   v=arccos   b=pi   n=+/-   m=0   ,=.(,)  .=.(,)

ESC=C/AC   RETURN=EXE/=   DELETE=delete the last number typed in

PSION+j/k/l/u/i/o  =  get the value of M1-M6

PSION+SHIFT+J/K/L/U/I/O  =  set the value of M1-M6 to the nr. displayd

PSION+c  =  check the display :-)


All functions will only work in DECimal-mode. You cannot make any calculations
in HEX or BIN. Press h to change mode DEC->HEX->BIN->DEC or shift-H to change
it back DEC<-HEX<-BIN<-DEC. Then you can calculate ,-)

It is not needed to close open brackets before pressing =/RETURN. If you close
a bracket, the expression between will be calculated and displayd.

If a error occurs, well, then you have type in something wrong, or the number
is to high ("Overflow"). 

Every function which needs one argument takes the number displayed, and
returns it to the display again.


Examples
--------

To calculate         type-in   display
--------------------------------------
5^2                   5            5
                      p            5
                      2            2
                      =           25
--------------------------------------
3*sqr(12)             3            3
                      *            3
                     12           12
                      r      3.464..
                      =     10.392..
--------------------------------------
6*6                   6            6
                      *            6    (not needed to type in 6 again!)
                      =           36
--------------------------------------display in first line:
3*(4+5+sin(7+2))      3            3    
                      *            3     3*
                      f or (       3     3*(
                      4            4     3*(
                      +            4     3*(4+
                      5            5     3*(4+
                      +            5     3*(4+5+
                      f or (       5     3*(4+5+(
                      7            7     3*(4+5+(
                      +            7     3*(4+5+(7+
                      2            2     3*(4+5+(7+
                      g or )       9     3*(4+5+
  (if RAD)            s      0.412..     3*(4+5+
                      =     28.236..     3*9.412..
----------------------------------------------------


Bugs & Limitations
------------------
Some limitations:

Max. Nr. to convert to binary is 255

Everything is calculated with OPL's   EVAL   - function
(Well, this _could_ be a limitation, don't know)

working with PI may not give correct results, e.g. sin(pi) is
displayed as -6.98..E-15  - and not as "0". I guess you know why...


